<!--
    Hand drawn to the Material Symbols Rounded grid rather than taken from the set,
    which is why it carries no license line and the others do.

    ## What it is a picture of

    Three rows, each a dot and a name. That is not a generic list glyph that happens to
    fit; it is the Areas list drawn small. An area is a colored dot beside a title on
    the Areas card, on the archive card, in the long press menu and on the manage screen
    this opens, so the glyph and the room agree about what an area looks like.

    ## Why not the obvious one, and why not the first thing drawn here

    design-v3.md section 15. The common glyph for a manage screen is a pencil, a gear or
    a slider set, and all three are taken or wrong: the gear is the settings glyph two
    positions along, the pencil is `edit`, and `tune` is already the edit-an-area glyph.

    The first version of this file drew two stacked cards, and on the device it read as
    a second archive box: the archive glyph beside it is a rounded rectangle with a
    horizontal line near its top, which is what a pair of stacked rounded rectangles at
    26dp also is. Two adjacent header glyphs a person cannot tell apart is worse than a
    familiar shape, so the dots carry the difference. Nothing else in the icon set has a
    filled circle in it.

    Stroked at 90 units on a 960 grid for the names, which measures the same weight as
    the outline symbols beside it; the dots are filled, as the real ones are.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="960"
    android:viewportHeight="960">
    <group
        android:translateX="0"
        android:translateY="960">
        <path
            android:fillColor="#FF000000"
            android:pathData="M235,-768 m-68,0 a68,68 0 1,0 136,0 a68,68 0 1,0 -136,0 z" />
        <path
            android:fillColor="#FF000000"
            android:pathData="M235,-480 m-68,0 a68,68 0 1,0 136,0 a68,68 0 1,0 -136,0 z" />
        <path
            android:fillColor="#FF000000"
            android:pathData="M235,-192 m-68,0 a68,68 0 1,0 136,0 a68,68 0 1,0 -136,0 z" />
        <path
            android:fillColor="#00000000"
            android:strokeColor="#FF000000"
            android:strokeWidth="90"
            android:strokeLineCap="round"
            android:pathData="M430,-768 L750,-768" />
        <path
            android:fillColor="#00000000"
            android:strokeColor="#FF000000"
            android:strokeWidth="90"
            android:strokeLineCap="round"
            android:pathData="M430,-480 L750,-480" />
        <path
            android:fillColor="#00000000"
            android:strokeColor="#FF000000"
            android:strokeWidth="90"
            android:strokeLineCap="round"
            android:pathData="M430,-192 L750,-192" />
    </group>
</vector>
